WEBVTT

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:19.686
I have a dream.

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:43.126
I'm a <i>butei</i>. Surrender now.

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:46.588
If I request an Amica contract with Aria...

00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:49.841
It's a two-man cell special
training system at our school.

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:52.927
When you combine the kanji for war
with the kanji for brothers or sisters,

00:00:52.927 --> 00:00:53.928
it is read Amica.

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:59.392
You receive special training directly
from an upperclassman for a year!

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.937
If you can defeat me, I'll agree
to the Amica contract with you.

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:06.524
Everyone should be given a chance equally.

00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:11.237
But... the results won't come out equally.
It's a matter of the effort you put in.

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:19.454
You passed the test.

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:20.246
What?

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:24.042
But you're not my official Amica yet.
You'll be in training.

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:29.297
You'll have to wait to make the official
contract until you get this gun back.

00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:32.384
Until then, you'll be
my assistant and do chores.

00:01:32.384 --> 00:01:33.551
Would that still be okay?

00:01:33.551 --> 00:01:36.846
Yes! Yes! Yes! Of course!

00:01:36.846 --> 00:01:39.307
As long as I can be with you, Aria!

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:42.894
Let's see... Which team are we fighting against?

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:44.437
Takachiho... Is that...

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.939
"1-C" "Takachiho"

00:01:49.651 --> 00:01:53.571
You're so pathetic. You call yourself a <i>butei</i>?

00:01:53.571 --> 00:01:56.783
Because Takachiho told me that I can't.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:57.909
You can't?

00:01:57.909 --> 00:02:01.746
That's the phrase you forbade me to use, so...

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.376
I'll be watching the match, too.

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:07.877
Make sure you win.

00:03:41.596 --> 00:03:43.431
Let's check for the last time.

00:03:43.431 --> 00:03:45.433
If we touch Team Takachiho's eye flag

00:03:45.433 --> 00:03:49.354
with our attack flag before
they touch ours, we win.

00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:53.525
As we discussed,
I buried our eye flag to hide it.

00:03:53.525 --> 00:03:57.278
As for the bee flags, please
hide yours under your clothes.

00:03:57.278 --> 00:04:01.700
We already did... since we can't use
them anymore once they get broken.

00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:08.206
Miss Mamiya and Miss Sasaki will attack.

00:04:08.206 --> 00:04:11.543
Raika and I will be in charge of defense.

00:04:11.543 --> 00:04:16.756
Miss Mamiya, our enemy may hide their
eye flag in a locked place like a locker.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.636
Yep. I brought a skeleton key with me.

00:04:23.513 --> 00:04:25.473
I ascertained our enemy's positions.

00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:27.809
It seems that they have an all-purpose key.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.979
Go on. What else did you find out?

00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:33.982
Akari Mamiya and Shino Sasaki are the attackers.

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:37.360
Looks like Raika Hino and
Kirin Shima will stay behind to defend.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.448
That's just what I thought.
You two take up your positions, too.

00:04:41.448 --> 00:04:43.116
Yes, Miss Urara!

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:47.829
Akari Mamiya... Can you make it to where I am?!

00:04:50.832 --> 00:04:52.834
Well then, Akari. Let's go.

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:54.085
Yep.

00:04:55.712 --> 00:05:00.842
Aria's watching me from somewhere.
I have to do my best.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:23.865
To get to the enemy lines, we have
no choice but to go through that street.

00:05:23.865 --> 00:05:25.617
Please watch out for ambushes.

00:05:25.617 --> 00:05:26.910
Okay.

00:05:32.707 --> 00:05:36.419
It's a town I'm used to,
but it looks eerie right now.

00:05:47.055 --> 00:05:48.556
Take this!

00:05:48.556 --> 00:05:49.516
Ugh!

00:05:49.516 --> 00:05:53.228
Akari!

00:05:53.228 --> 00:05:53.895
Ah!

00:05:53.895 --> 00:05:54.771
You...

00:05:54.771 --> 00:05:55.939
...thieving cat!

00:05:55.939 --> 00:05:57.440
What?!

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:06.825
A two-on-one fight...

00:06:12.288 --> 00:06:14.040
I trained especially for that!

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.417
Akari!

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.921
Leave them to me! You go on!

00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:21.464
But...!

00:06:21.464 --> 00:06:22.966
Let's win!

00:06:31.766 --> 00:06:34.602
"Pedestrians and Bicycles"

00:06:43.862 --> 00:06:46.823
Hello, Kirin? This is Akari!

00:06:46.823 --> 00:06:48.658
What's the matter, Miss Mamiya?

00:06:48.658 --> 00:06:51.953
We ran into the Aizawa sisters.
I broke through alone!

00:06:51.953 --> 00:06:55.290
Shino's holding them back for me.
What's going on over there?

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:56.916
Nothing right now.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:59.919
Got it. I'm heading to the enemy lines!

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:04.466
Roger. The twins used guerrilla tactics.

00:07:04.466 --> 00:07:09.304
Assuming one would defend...
there may be another attacker out there.

00:07:09.304 --> 00:07:10.096
You're right.

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.181
Ah!

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:14.267
That is me.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:16.061
Hina Fuma!

00:07:20.315 --> 00:07:22.942
As I thought, she's hard to deal with.

00:07:33.912 --> 00:07:35.830
As big sister, I'll protect my little sister.

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.248
Raika...!

00:07:37.248 --> 00:07:40.335
Shima... your hands are dirty.

00:07:40.335 --> 00:07:43.046
You must've buried the
eye flag somewhere nearby.

00:07:44.005 --> 00:07:46.049
You have good eyes.

00:07:46.049 --> 00:07:49.761
But you should...

00:07:49.761 --> 00:07:51.221
...focus those eyes on me!

00:07:51.221 --> 00:07:53.515
Eyes are meant to be deceived.

00:07:56.518 --> 00:07:58.186
I can't see!

00:08:06.444 --> 00:08:08.196
Raika!

00:08:33.555 --> 00:08:36.641
Hello, it's me.

00:08:36.641 --> 00:08:38.476
Yeah, that's right.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.814
There's something I want you to help me with.

00:08:42.814 --> 00:08:44.899
Yeah. Thanks.

00:09:07.797 --> 00:09:10.091
So you're the one who came...

00:09:12.677 --> 00:09:16.139
I wonder if this is also our fate.

00:09:16.139 --> 00:09:18.725
Urara Takachiho...

00:09:18.725 --> 00:09:23.730
I'm glad... that I'll be able to...

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:25.940
...bring you down with my own hands.

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:30.153
Sturm Ruger Super Redhawk...!

00:09:46.252 --> 00:09:50.674
You're wasting your time hiding.
I can cause as much destruction as I want,

00:09:50.674 --> 00:09:52.801
since I'll just have to pay for the damage.

00:10:13.988 --> 00:10:17.158
This isn't working. She's outside
the range of the Micro-Uzi.

00:10:49.691 --> 00:10:51.192
Can you see them?

00:10:53.528 --> 00:10:55.739
I've got a great view.

00:10:55.739 --> 00:10:58.116
I knew they'd fight here.

00:10:58.116 --> 00:11:00.035
Considering Takachii's personality,

00:11:00.035 --> 00:11:04.330
I thought she'd pick a place where
she could shoot that huge gun recklessly.

00:11:05.415 --> 00:11:08.418
Well, let's relax and watch the show,

00:11:08.418 --> 00:11:11.880
as I took the trouble
to arrange things for them.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:14.090
Be careful not to be conspicuous.

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:17.218
If they see you, things will get complicated.

00:11:17.218 --> 00:11:19.471
I know. I know.

00:11:30.482 --> 00:11:31.566
Raika!

00:11:31.566 --> 00:11:35.779
Stay put no matter what!
Or I won't be able to tell where you are!

00:11:35.779 --> 00:11:37.572
O-Okay!

00:11:39.574 --> 00:11:43.036
You're talking while I'm attacking you?

00:11:43.036 --> 00:11:45.288
You're awfully confident, aren't you?

00:11:45.955 --> 00:11:48.750
You think so? Then take this!

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:50.627
A confident blow!

00:11:52.045 --> 00:11:55.382
Confidence is something
that ultimately gets destroyed.

00:12:00.261 --> 00:12:06.935
You know... I requested an
Amica contract with Aria Kanzaki.

00:12:06.935 --> 00:12:07.894
Huh?

00:12:07.894 --> 00:12:12.649
But I failed the test to become her Amica.

00:12:12.649 --> 00:12:17.904
After that, I offered quite a bit of money,

00:12:17.904 --> 00:12:21.199
but she didn't say yes.

00:12:23.702 --> 00:12:25.412
But now...

00:12:26.788 --> 00:12:29.249
...I feel that...

00:12:30.458 --> 00:12:32.836
...it was actually good...

00:12:33.878 --> 00:12:36.131
...that I didn't become her Amica.

00:12:38.383 --> 00:12:43.013
She made a hopeless E Rank
<i>butei </i>like you her Amica.

00:12:43.013 --> 00:12:46.599
I can't help but think that she went mad.

00:12:46.599 --> 00:12:53.815
Any way you look at it,
it's obvious that I'm far superior to you.

00:12:53.815 --> 00:12:56.067
Aria Kanzaki...

00:12:56.067 --> 00:12:59.654
She doesn't seem as good as her reputation!

00:13:33.021 --> 00:13:36.066
I don't care what you say about me.

00:13:36.066 --> 00:13:37.233
Hmm?

00:13:37.233 --> 00:13:39.944
But...

00:13:39.944 --> 00:13:42.572
...don't speak ill of Aria!

00:13:54.084 --> 00:13:57.796
How was it? Did it hurt?

00:13:57.796 --> 00:14:00.715
What... power...

00:14:05.512 --> 00:14:09.391
Next, I'll target a spot
that causes even more pain.

00:14:14.562 --> 00:14:15.855
Akari...

00:14:18.024 --> 00:14:21.236
Falling back was the wrong move, Akari Mamiya.

00:14:21.236 --> 00:14:24.280
When it comes to guns,
the effective range is important.

00:14:25.824 --> 00:14:30.829
At this distance, your
Uzi's targeting is random.

00:14:34.082 --> 00:14:36.793
As opposed to my gun...

00:14:36.793 --> 00:14:41.089
...which can fire bullets
precisely where I want.

00:14:44.426 --> 00:14:46.594
Be flexible when you fight.

00:14:50.473 --> 00:14:55.270
Maybe it's about time to
blow you up along with the bicycles.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:56.938
Ah!

00:14:56.938 --> 00:14:59.107
Be flexible.

00:15:03.486 --> 00:15:04.988
Hm?

00:15:14.956 --> 00:15:17.042
Ah! Shoot!

00:15:17.042 --> 00:15:20.295
Sorry, whoever owns this scooter!
Let me use it just for one minute!

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:27.802
Still, people can be killed by those
bullets when they're hit in the head.

00:15:27.802 --> 00:15:33.975
Being told that makes me want to do it.

00:15:33.975 --> 00:15:35.894
Fall off!

00:15:35.894 --> 00:15:38.730
My training prepared me for this...

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.899
I'm not gonna fall off!

00:15:40.899 --> 00:15:43.151
It's all set now!

00:15:45.779 --> 00:15:47.155
Oof!

00:15:51.493 --> 00:15:52.994
Please run!

00:15:52.994 --> 00:15:55.830
Hold on a sec. We can't leave our eye flag here!

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:58.249
Don't worry about it! Hurry!

00:15:58.917 --> 00:16:00.377
What?

00:16:06.508 --> 00:16:09.678
Ah! That's... their attack flag!

00:16:18.269 --> 00:16:19.938
I won't let you shoot.

00:16:21.523 --> 00:16:23.024
Come on...

00:16:26.027 --> 00:16:27.362
Make it!

00:16:29.197 --> 00:16:32.283
Go!

00:16:41.626 --> 00:16:43.420
We did it...

00:16:44.462 --> 00:16:48.049
This can't be... happening...

00:16:51.553 --> 00:16:54.597
Ow...

00:16:54.597 --> 00:16:56.683
We did it.

00:16:56.683 --> 00:16:59.894
We did it, Akari! We did it!

00:16:59.894 --> 00:17:03.106
Yeah! We did it!

00:17:03.106 --> 00:17:05.859
We really did it, didn't we?!

00:17:05.859 --> 00:17:09.404
I... lost...?

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:19.039
"Yellow Peach"

00:17:22.292 --> 00:17:23.585
We did it!

00:17:23.585 --> 00:17:27.422
We did it! Sounds like Miss Mamiya
and Miss Sasaki did it!

00:17:27.422 --> 00:17:29.841
What? This isn't the time to rejoice.

00:17:29.841 --> 00:17:33.386
They might've gotten to our eye flag, too.

00:17:33.386 --> 00:17:37.349
If that's the case, the rules say it's a draw.

00:17:37.349 --> 00:17:39.976
In order to deceive one's enemy,
one must first deceive one's allies.

00:17:39.976 --> 00:17:43.438
What I buried was a bee flag,
which they could go ahead and take.

00:17:43.438 --> 00:17:46.441
And... I've got the eye flag here.

00:17:47.067 --> 00:17:48.485
Huh?

00:17:50.612 --> 00:17:53.448
I hate bees.

00:18:29.234 --> 00:18:31.736
I-I can't get out!

00:18:31.736 --> 00:18:34.739
--Uhm... Are you okay?
--Stupid barrel!

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:46.084
Can you hear me?

00:18:46.084 --> 00:18:47.627
Akari...

00:19:21.536 --> 00:19:22.912
What?

00:19:26.833 --> 00:19:28.209
Huh?

00:20:07.165 --> 00:20:10.001
A-Are you okay?

00:20:10.001 --> 00:20:12.170
Ahh...

00:20:16.174 --> 00:20:19.719
Akari! Are you okay?!

00:20:19.719 --> 00:20:21.930
Y-Yeah...

00:20:26.017 --> 00:20:29.104
Ah! Aria!

00:20:29.104 --> 00:20:32.857
I knew it was you who saved us!

00:20:32.857 --> 00:20:35.694
Don't thank me, thank Reki.

00:20:35.694 --> 00:20:37.529
Thank you very much!

00:20:41.449 --> 00:20:43.493
That was really close.

00:20:43.493 --> 00:20:47.455
That's because they ran
amok in a place like this.

00:20:47.455 --> 00:20:52.210
Good grief, we're gonna have
to write tons of reports about this.

00:20:55.005 --> 00:20:56.172
Are you okay?!

00:20:56.172 --> 00:20:58.299
Are you hurt?!

00:21:01.386 --> 00:21:02.345
Let's go.

00:21:02.345 --> 00:21:03.930
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:09.728 --> 00:21:13.189
--We did it!
--You were wonderful, Raika!

00:21:13.189 --> 00:21:17.652
Do you know that "someone who's
popular also attracts incidents"?

00:21:17.652 --> 00:21:19.988
I'm glad that I asked you to come.

00:21:19.988 --> 00:21:24.325
I never thought that something
like this would happen, though.

00:21:24.325 --> 00:21:26.077
What do you think?

00:21:26.077 --> 00:21:28.496
Was it a coincidence? Or...

00:21:35.337 --> 00:21:38.506
If it wasn't a coincidence...

00:21:41.343 --> 00:21:44.846
--Wow, we really did it!
--So you came running here, huh?!

00:21:46.806 --> 00:21:48.683
That was interesting!

00:21:48.683 --> 00:21:54.647
Hm? I see my scooter over there. I wonder why...

00:21:54.647 --> 00:21:56.441
That's so blatant.

00:21:58.526 --> 00:22:00.236
Are you a villain...?

00:22:03.615 --> 00:22:06.034
Or are you just softhearted?

00:22:06.034 --> 00:22:08.078
"Episode 5: Quartet, Part 2"

00:22:08.078 --> 00:22:10.997
"Episode 5: Quartet, Part 2"
Maybe both.

00:23:41.629 --> 00:23:43.631
Giving derringer training in CVR?

00:23:43.631 --> 00:23:47.177
I've got some small, cute classmates.
Please give us lessons.

00:23:47.177 --> 00:23:49.346
I wonder if she has some reason for this...

00:23:49.346 --> 00:23:52.474
They really are too close.

00:23:54.142 --> 00:23:55.310
Do it.

00:23:55.310 --> 00:23:56.160
"Episode 6: Little Devils' Request"
